  "contentHtml": "<h1 class=\"module-heading\">Chapter 10: Issues</h1>\n<div class=\"card\"><h2 class=\"card-title\">Purpose and place in PRINCE2</h2><p>The issues practice helps the project manager record, assess and control matters that need a decision. These include problems or concerns, external events, business opportunities, requests for change and off specifications. Change control protects approved product baselines. Assess effects on benefits, cost, time, quality, scope, risk and sustainability; seek the decision from the appropriate delegated authority.</p></div>\n<div class=\"scenario-box\"><h2>SnakeBite: a decision and its consequence</h2><p>Maya proposes a two player mode after the scope is approved. Tomek discovers that the ranking API misses its agreed response time. Zosia logs the first as a request for change and the second as an off specification. She assesses their impact and recommends action in an issue report. Tomek waits for an authorized decision before building the extra feature. Available change budget alone does not approve the work.</p></div>\n<figure class=\"study-figure\"><div class=\"study-flow\"><div class=\"study-step\"><span>1</span><strong>Record in issue register</strong></div><div class=\"study-step\"><span>2</span><strong>Assess impact; issue report if needed</strong></div><div class=\"study-step\"><span>3</span><strong>Authorized decision or escalation</strong></div><div class=\"study-step\"><span>4</span><strong>Implement; update product status</strong></div></div><figcaption><strong>Read the flow:</strong> A recorded request is not an approved change. Escalate beyond delegated authority or forecast tolerance.</figcaption></figure>\n<div class=\"card\"><h2 class=\"card-title\">Exam terms and management products</h2><p><strong>Request for change:</strong> proposal to change an approved baseline. <strong>Off specification:</strong> something agreed is not, or is forecast not to be, delivered. <strong>Risk:</strong> an uncertain future event; an issue needs attention now. <strong>Concession:</strong> authorized acceptance of an off specification without corrective action.</p><p>The <strong>issue register</strong> tracks formal issues and decisions; an <strong>issue report</strong> records detailed analysis and a recommendation; the <strong>product register</strong> tracks versions and status. The <strong>change budget</strong> funds approved changes under agreed rules. An agile backlog does not confer change authority.</p></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h2 class=\"card-title\">Issue types and the change decision</h2><p><strong>Problem or concern:</strong> a matter requiring attention, such as a team conflict or a defect affecting delivery. <strong>External event:</strong> an event outside the project requiring a response. <strong>Business opportunity:</strong> a possible change that could add value. <strong>Request for change:</strong> a proposal to alter an approved baseline. <strong>Off specification:</strong> something agreed has not been or will not be delivered as specified. A possible future supplier outage belongs in the risk register until it occurs or creates an issue that must be addressed.</p><p>The issue management approach defines how matters are recorded, analyzed and decided. For a material change, Zosia checks the effect on benefits, cost, time, quality, scope, risk and sustainability; she also checks any funding in the change budget and the limits of delegated change authority. The executive or board may need to decide if the effect crosses a delegated limit or threatens the business case. When a forecast exceeds the stage tolerance, the project manager escalates using an exception report.</p><p>The project log can include an issue register and daily log. The issue register tracks formal issues and their status. An issue report contains detailed assessment and options for significant matters. The product register shows the current status and approvals of affected products; product descriptions establish their agreed criteria. A risk register is for uncertain events and is not interchangeable with the issue register. Decisions and baseline updates are recorded so that implementers work against the correct approved version.</p></div><figure class=\"study-figure\"><div class=\"study-flow\"><div class=\"study-step\"><span>1</span><strong>Maya requests a feature</strong></div><div class=\"study-step\"><span>2</span><strong>Zosia logs and assesses it</strong></div><div class=\"study-step\"><span>3</span><strong>Authorized role decides</strong></div><div class=\"study-step\"><span>4</span><strong>Tomek delivers approved work</strong></div></div><figcaption><strong>Read this decision flow:</strong> A request is not approval. The change budget provides funds only when the authorized role approves the change and its effect on the baseline.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"card quiz-section\"><h2 class=\"card-title\">SnakeBite story: review the decisions</h2><div id=\"m11-story-quiz\"></div></div><div class=\"hard-knowledge-header\"><div class=\"hard-knowledge-title\">Foundation exam practice</div></div><div class=\"quiz-section\"><div id=\"m11-exam-quiz\"></div></div><div class=\"flashcards-container\" id=\"m11-flashcards\"></div>",
